From 9b4f2c7d1e6a3805d2c4f1b7a9e0c6d3b8f5a2e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2026 14:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ucode: do not touch the freed VM after hostapd_ucode_free()

hostapd's main() (hostapd/main.c, "out:" label as patched by
601-ucode_support.patch) tears the ucode VM down first and only then
deinitializes the interfaces:

  out:
	hostapd_ucode_free();
	hostapd_global_ctrl_iface_deinit(&interfaces);
	for (i = 0; i < interfaces.count; i++)
		hostapd_interface_deinit_free(interfaces.iface[i]);

hostapd_ucode_free() (src/ap/ucode.c:880-885) runs the script's
"shutdown" callback and then wpa_ucode_free_vm() (src/utils/ucode.c:493)
-> uc_vm_free() -> ucv_freeall(), which frees every value the VM ever
owned, including the bss_registry and iface_registry arrays created in
hostapd_ucode_init() (:861-865). wpa_ucode_free_vm() only clears the
utils-side "registry" pointer; the ap-side statics vm, global,
bss_registry and iface_registry keep pointing at freed memory.

That is fine for OpenWrt's own use, where every interface was added by
hostapd.uc and the "shutdown" callback removes them all through
hostapd.remove_iface() while the VM is still alive, so nothing is left
for the loop below. It is not fine for interfaces that were added
through the control interface or the command line (pWHM starts one
global hostapd with the radio configs on the command line and ADDs the
rest over /var/run/hostapd/global): hostapd.data.config knows nothing
about them, "shutdown" leaves them alone, and the deinit loop then
runs, for every BSS that is still started:

  hostapd_interface_deinit_free() -> hostapd_interface_deinit()
    -> hostapd_bss_deinit() -> hostapd_free_hapd_data() (hostapd.c:503)
      -> hostapd_ucode_free_bss() (src/ap/ucode.c:908-926)
        -> wpa_ucode_registry_remove(bss_registry, idx) (utils/ucode.c:465)
          -> wpa_ucode_registry_get() -> ucv_array_get(bss_registry, ..)
            -> ucv_type(bss_registry)        <- freed array

and, via hostapd_interface_free() -> hostapd_cleanup_iface()
(hostapd.c:770), hostapd_ucode_free_iface() on the freed iface_registry
for every interface. Depending on what happened to the freed pages this
is a plain read of freed memory, a SIGSEGV in libucode's ucv_type()
when musl's mallocng already unmapped the group the array lived in, or
heap corruption (ucv_array_set() on a recycled chunk) that surfaces
later as a crash in free().

Observed on a prplOS/pWHM build (hostapd 2024-09-15, ucode 2025-07-18,
musl 1.2.5) whenever pWHM stops the last active radio: it sends
TERMINATE over the global control socket while that radio's BSSes are
still started, and 10-20 ms later hostapd dies with
"segfault at 7f...490 ip ... in libucode.so.20230711" (ucv_type,
"mov (%rdi),%al") or "segfault at 10 ... in libc.so" (mallocng
get_meta() from free()). The faulting address sat at the same offset
below libucode's mapping in three of four crashes, i.e. it was the same
early allocation each time.

OpenWrt main (601-ucode_support.patch, package/network/services/hostapd/
src/src/ap/ucode.c as of 2026-09-25) has the same main() ordering and
the same unguarded hooks, so this is reachable upstream with any
non-script-managed interface too.

Fix: after wpa_ucode_free_vm(), drop the stale ap-side pointers and
make hostapd_ucode_free_bss()/hostapd_ucode_free_iface() no-ops once
the VM is gone. The other hooks are already safe: hostapd_ucode_bss_cb()
and the sta hooks go through wpa_ucode_call_prepare(), which bails out
on the cleared utils registry before touching any value. The script's
"shutdown" callback keeps running first, so OpenWrt's own teardown is
unchanged; the BSSes it did not know about simply get no "bss_remove"
event at exit, which nothing consumes at that point anyway.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/ucode.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -882,10 +882,25 @@
 	if (wpa_ucode_call_prepare("shutdown") == 0)
 		ucv_put(wpa_ucode_call(0));
 	wpa_ucode_free_vm();
+
+	/* The VM and every value it owned (bss_registry, iface_registry,
+	 * global) are gone now. hostapd's main() calls hostapd_ucode_free()
+	 * before it deinitializes the interfaces, so the per-BSS/per-iface
+	 * hooks below can still run after this point for any interface that
+	 * was not removed by the "shutdown" script callback. Drop the stale
+	 * pointers so those hooks become no-ops instead of touching freed
+	 * memory. */
+	vm = NULL;
+	global = NULL;
+	bss_registry = NULL;
+	iface_registry = NULL;
 }
 
 void hostapd_ucode_free_iface(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 {
+	if (!iface_registry)
+		return;
+
 	ucv_put(wpa_ucode_registry_remove(iface_registry, iface->ucode.idx));
 }
 
@@ -909,6 +924,11 @@
 {
 	uc_value_t *val;
 
+	if (!bss_registry) {
+		hapd->ucode.idx = 0;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	val = wpa_ucode_registry_remove(bss_registry, hapd->ucode.idx);
 	if (!val)
 		return;
-- 
